(locally) orientation-preserving must be the following:\n\n![](images/53/5389d4bb3047ce09fdd363b74f11656401529f5385409f693c18a1c20cac51ec.png)" 13194139535917 17592186045443 true] [17592186541391 1080 "images/89/898fd878de4c411294f1949a767f28c2b5d8b2f8c4f9096b5f78835fd51c31f7.png" 13194139535917 17592186045443 true] [17592186541391 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 13194139535917 17592186045443 true] [17592186541391 1083 #uuid "b90f54e8-d871-567f-b5dd-68883fc7cf68" 13194139535917 17592186045443 true] [17592186541392 1080 "images/6d/6d3dd3fffbd04ef723ec8bb0701747d5d7f973a23d2ecfdf0437f8827a6e0cec.png" 13194139535917 17592186045443 true] [17592186541392 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 13194139535917 17592186045443 true] [17592186541392 1083 #uuid "c2885d29-2182-5713-9c10-f79670914ca1" 13194139535917 17592186045443 true] [17592186541393 1068 #edb/ref 17592186541349 13194139535917 17592186045443 true] [17592186541393 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139535917 17592186045443 true] [17592186541393 1071 "Which of the following shows the region in the $uv$-plane where the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\left(u + 1\\right)^{2} \\\\ 3 v + 3\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nis (locally) orientation-preserving?" 13194139535917 17592186045443 true] [17592186541393 1072 #uuid "c4fbb398-85ee-59ed-888e-83228cf28f5c" 13194139535917 17592186045443 true] [17592186541393 1074 "Recall that a transformation is (locally) orientation-preserving at the points where the Jacobian determinant is positive:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}>0\n$$\n\nWe have\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\left(u + 1\\right)^{2} \\\\ 3 v + 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} &=\\begin{vmatrix}8 u + 8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ &=(8 u + 8)\\cdot (3)-(0)\\cdot (0) \\\\ &=24 u + 24.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the required regions, we solve the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}24 u + 24 &>0 \\\\ u > -1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the equation\n\n$$\nu = -1\n$$\n\ndefines a vertical line.\n\nTherefore, the region where the transformation is (locally) orientation-preserving must be the following:\n\n![](images/b9/b99527183109e4b5f9e870ddd4f0e2738f2642b22038990272263926155e7256.png)" 13194139535917 17592186045443 true] [17592186541394 1075 #edb/ref 17592186541355 13194139535917 17592186045443 true] [17592186541394 1075 #edb/ref 17592186541360 13194139535917 17592186045443 true] [17592186541394 1075 #edb/ref 17592186541400 13194139535917 17592186045443 true] [17592186541394 1075 #edb/ref 17592186541409 13194139535917 17592186045443 true] [17592186541394 1075 #edb/ref 17592186541411 13194139535917 17592186045443 true] [17592186541394 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139535917 17592186045443 true] [17592186541394 1077 "selection" 13194139535917 17592186045443 true] [17592186541394 1078 #edb/ref 17592186541360 13194139535917 17592186045443 true] [17592186541394 1079 #uuid "c5bba0f6-32b6-5eda-9fcf-43279157826a" 13194139535917 17592186045443 true] [17592186541395 1068 #edb/ref 17592186541378 13194139535917 17592186045443 true] [17592186541395 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139535917 17592186045443 true] [17592186541395 1071 "Which of the following shows the region in the $uv$-plane where the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}v + \\left(u + 3\\right)^{2} + 1 \\\\ - 3 u - \\left(v + 1\\right)^{2} - 9\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nis (locally) orientation-reversing?" 13194139535917 17592186045443 true] [17592186541395 1072 #uuid "c602b91c-8162-5ddc-91d0-b31b9b87f5e1" 13194139535917 17592186045443 true] [17592186541395 1074 "Recall that a transformation is (locally) orientation-reversing at the points where the Jacobian determinant is negative:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}<0\n$$\n\nWe have\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}v + \\left(u + 3\\right)^{2} + 1 \\\\ - 3 u - \\left(v + 1\\right)^{2} - 9\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} &=\\begin{vmatrix}2 u + 6 & 1 \\\\ -3 & - 2 v - 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ &=(2 u + 6)\\cdot (- 2 v - 2)-(1)\\cdot (-3) \\\\ &=- 4 u v - 4 u - 12 v - 9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the required regions, we solve the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}- 4 u v - 4 u - 12 v - 9 &<0 \\\\ \\left(u + 3\\right) \\left(v + 1\\right) > \\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the solution $v > -1 + \\frac{3}{4 \\left(u + 3\\right)}$ for $u>-3$ and $v < -1 + \\frac{3}{4 \\left(u + 3\\right)}$ for $u<-3.$ At $u=-3,$ the Jacobian is positive, so this line is excluded from the required region.\n\nNotice that the equation\n\n$$\nv = -1 + \\frac{3}{4 \\left(u + 3\\right)}\n$$\n\ndefines a hyperbola.\n\nTherefore, the region where the transformation is (locally) orientation-reversing must be the following:\n\n![](images/a1/a14192698baa5f54314d4325bcbc3e9d488ec728b0beee1570921e0869259da3.png)" 13194139535917 17592186045443 true] [17592186541396 1080 "images/a7/a7ba4a937a154e28f17d2786c9d96fa61319e58e55f5cde4739738a18244f9dd.png" 13194139535917 17592186045443 true] [17592186541396 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 13194139535917 17592186045443 true] [17592186541396 1083 #uuid "c702b198-4176-5491-be20-71307ad8580b" 13194139535917 17592186045443 true] [17592186541397 1075 #edb/ref 17592186541358 13194139535917 17592186045443 true] [17592186541397 1075 #edb/ref 17592186541366 13194139535917 17592186045443 true] [17592186541397 1075 #edb/ref 17592186541369 13194139535917 17592186045443 true] [17592186541397 1075 #edb/ref 17592186541372 13194139535917 17592186045443 true] [17592186541397 1075 #edb/ref 17592186541385 13194139535917 17592186045443 true] [17592186541397 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139535917 17592186045443 true] [17592186541397 1077 "selection" 131941395